#Референс_PromptPilot_Runner_Patterns<[
Базис:
  PromptPilot is a practical runner layer for AI CLI tools: interfaces enqueue work, a worker polls a SQLite/WAL queue, providers map to command templates, and results are visible in web or Telegram UI.
  Work Graph already has a stronger source-of-truth model: WorkItem state, Worker Input/Output v1, Evidence v1 and policy-gated transitions.
  Therefore PromptPilot is a reference for runner mechanics, not a replacement state model.
Вектор:
  Adopt queue/worker separation as an implementation boundary: UI, scheduler and integrations propose runnable work, while a worker performs one bounded run and returns structured output.
  Keep provider registry ideas: provider id, command/API capability, model/options, timeout, cost/log extraction and capability flags, but map them into providerHints and selection policy rather than task state.
  Adopt scheduling, pause/resume, retry and rate-limit handling as runner concerns: nextRunAt, retryCount, exponential backoff with jitter, timeout and crash recovery produce worker-run/blocker evidence.
  Treat task result UI as an operator dashboard pattern: show status, run summary, logs, provider, cost/tokens when available, artifacts, evidence and proposed transition.
  Consider SQLite/WAL only as a derived runner queue/cache for runnable projections and durable run logs; .bvc Work Graph remains canonical.
Цель:
  Work Graph runner layer should gain practical scheduling and provider execution mechanics without becoming a prompt queue whose database owns project truth.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: promptpilot-runner-patterns
  work.source: analyze-promptpilot-task-runner-reference
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Паттерны_Взять<[
Базис:
  PromptPilot separates interfaces, queue, worker and providers clearly enough to keep runner operations observable.
Вектор:
  Queue/worker separation: use a small runner queue only for executable WorkItem projections, not for authoring or deciding Work Graph state.
  Provider registry: record provider command/API adapter, capabilities, model/options, timeout, structured log support and rate-limit detection.
  Scheduling: support run-after time, recurring task proposals and worker pause/resume as runtime controls.
  Retry/rate-limit: detect known rate-limit failures, compute exponential backoff with jitter, cap retries and record retry evidence before requeue.
  Crash recovery: recover abandoned running projections to retryable state with evidence that the previous run was interrupted.
  Result UI: surface provider, run duration, cost/tokens if available, logs, artifacts, patch summary and transition proposal.
  Optional integrations: Telegram, tray and notifications are useful operator channels but should remain adapters above the runner core.
Цель:
  Reuse PromptPilot's operational lessons while keeping Work Graph contracts provider-neutral and evidence-first.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  reference.id: promptpilot-patterns-to-adopt
  decision.id: promptpilot-runner-patterns
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Паттерны_Не_Брать_Или_Отложить<[
Базис:
  PromptPilot optimizes for prompt execution through external CLI tools, while Work Graph optimizes for project state, evidence and decisions.
Вектор:
  Do not make the queue or SQLite database the source of truth for tasks; it is only a derived dispatch/log layer.
  Do not model WorkItems as prompt-only records; WorkItem keeps role, dependencies, target files, DoD, evidence, trace refs and transition policy.
  Do not store provider-specific session state as business state; session_id/resume tokens are transient run metadata and must not be required to understand project status.
  Defer Telegram, tray, mobile reply flows, recurring tasks and cost dashboard until runner core and operator dashboard snapshot exist.
  Defer provider-specific skill discovery until provider registry capabilities need it; it must not leak Claude-only concepts into Worker Input v1.
  Avoid unsafe skip-permissions style controls as defaults; Work Graph policy remains deny-by-default with explicit tool/network/file-write capabilities.
Цель:
  Prevent a useful runner reference from weakening Work Graph's canonical state, safety and evidence boundaries.

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  rule.id: promptpilot-patterns-deferred-or-rejected
  decision.id: promptpilot-runner-patterns
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Маппинг_WorkGraph_Runner_Layer<[
Базис:
  Existing contracts already define Worker Input v1, Worker Output v1 and Evidence Record v1.
Вектор:
  WorkItem -> runnable projection: scheduler selects a ready/in_progress task from current Work Graph snapshot and creates a runner queue item with task id, runId, nextRunAt, provider requirements and policy hash.
  Runnable projection -> Worker Input: runtime rebuilds task snapshot, memorySlice, allowedTools, targetFiles, policy and providerHints from canonical state immediately before execution.
  Provider run: selected provider adapter executes CLI/API/local runner with bounded timeout, cancellation and tool policy.
  Provider result -> Worker Output: adapter returns status, patchSummary, evidence array, logs, failureReason, retryAdvice and transitionRequest.
  Worker Output -> Evidence: runtime normalizes worker-run, command/test/file/change/blocker records using Evidence v1 fields.
  Evidence -> transition proposal: Work Graph runtime applies gates; success can move to verify/done, rate-limit can schedule retry, repeated failure can block, and needs_human can request operator input.
  Dashboard snapshot: UI reads Work Graph and runner log projection to show current run, queue, evidence, retry state and proposed next action.
Цель:
  The runner becomes an execution projection around Work Graph, not an independent task manager.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: promptpilot-workgraph-runner-mapping
  decision.id: promptpilot-runner-patterns
  trace.status: verified
]>

#MVP_Recommendation_And_Deferrals<[
Базис:
  The current local runner proves Worker Input/Output shape but does not yet cover durable scheduling, retry or provider registry.
Вектор:
  MVP next step: add a minimal runner registry/config shape with provider id, type, command/API adapter, capabilities, timeout and rate-limit classifier.
  MVP next step: add a derived runner log or queue projection with runId, taskId, providerId, status, nextRunAt, retryCount, startedAt, finishedAt and evidence ids.
  MVP next step: implement retry/rate-limit evidence semantics before adding remote channels.
  MVP next step: feed runner records into operator dashboard snapshot rather than building a separate PromptPilot-like task UI.
  Deferred: Telegram bot, tray exe, mobile reply/resume flow, recurring tasks, cost aggregation and provider skill discovery.
  Deferred storage choice: SQLite/WAL is attractive for local durable queue/logs, but choose it only after serialization/runtime substrate decisions confirm it as a derived cache.
Цель:
  Ship scheduling and provider execution reliability first; add operator conveniences after Work Graph remains visibly in control.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: promptpilot-runner-mvp-scope
